.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount
function reads a file stream and counts its lines, words, and characters.
.PP
The resulting counts are stored in the integer variables pointed to by
.I lines,
.I words,
and
.I chars.
.PP
The function returns 0 on success and -1 if an invalid argument is supplied.
